      {
        "variation": "default",
        "version": "initial",
        "items": [],
        "primary": {
          "eyebrow": "The project",
          "title": "Built to tour the world",
          "body": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "An orchestrion is a band of acoustic instruments played by machine. Pat Metheny plays alongside it on stage: the instruments respond to his playing and his arrangements, night after night, in a different hall every evening.",
              "spans": []
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "That asks a lot of an instrument. It has to travel, survive set-up and breakdown, and play with the timing and dynamics of a jazz musician.",
              "spans": []
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The orchestrion stayed with him for many productions. When he last played in Belgium, at BOZAR in Brussels, it was on stage with him.",
              "spans": []
            }
          ],
          "image": {},
          "video": {
            "link_type": "Media"
          },
